REM Protects a multi-line DEF FN whose body is never explicitly closed from
REM being misparsed into fallback expression statements and flagged for a
REM missing line break: a closed function still ends at its own closing
REM marker below, a statement after that marker stays its own top-level
REM statement, and the final unclosed function's body runs cleanly to the
REM end of the file with no diagnostic.
DEF FNADDONE(num)
sum = num + 1
RETURN sum
FNEND
total = 1
def fntriple(val)
doubled = val + val
tripled = doubled + val
return tripled
